.\" tc08(1) manual page
.TH TC08 1 "December 2025" "waffle8" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
tc08 \- TC08 DECtape controller (device 076/077) for the PDP\-8 emulator
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
The controller is attached automatically when creating the host simulator board
or by linking
.B src/emulator/tc08_device.c
into
.BR factory/libpdp8.so .
Unit images are configured via environment:
.IP
.EX
export TC08_IMAGE0=media/tape0.tu56        # read\-only
export TC08_IMAGE1=media/tape1.tu56        # read/write
python3 tools/webdp8.py                    # or any host using libpdp8.so
.EE
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The TC08 emulation provides a minimal DECtape data channel with two units
(device code 076 plus the alternate code 077 for DTXA). It requires physical
frame images (129-word frames stored in .tu56 format) and assembles each OS/8
logical transfer from two consecutive frames. Unit 0 is read-only by default;
unit 1 is writable and will be created on demand when an image path is
supplied. Each image is zero-extended to 1101 physical frames on load so a
full tape’s worth of blocks is always present, and writable units persist the
padding to disk the next time they flush.
.
.SH IOT INSTRUCTIONS
Device code
.B 076
unless noted; octal encodings shown.
.TP
.B DCR \- 6762
Device clear/reset. Sets controller ready; clears transfer address and block.
.TP
.B DTSF \- 6764
Skip if ready. Power\-up/reset leaves the device ready so the bootstrap loop
will skip.
.TP
.B DTLB \- 6766
Load block number and start transfer. The AC format:
.RS
.IP "\fBbits 0\-9\fR" 6
Logical block number.
.IP "\fBbit 10\fR" 6
Unit select (0=unit0, 1=unit1).
.IP "\fBbit 11\fR" 6
Write flag (1=write core to tape, 0=read tape to core).
.RE
Uses the previously loaded transfer address. On success sets ready and issues a
skip; on error sets error (bit 1) and does not skip.
.TP
.B GO \- 6767
Defined but unused in the minimal model; transfers begin on DTLB.
.TP
.B DTXA \- 6771 (device 077)
Load transfer address from AC.
.
.SH DATA TRANSFER
Every transfer moves 256 consecutive words by stitching two physical frames
together (128 data words per frame; checksum words are cleared on writes).
Reads and writes wrap at core size. Images must already be physical frame
layouts: writes are rejected if the unit is read-only or the controller cannot
extend the backing store.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TC08_IMAGE0
Path to the unit0 DECtape image (default
.BR media/tape0.tu56 ).
Read\-only.
.TP
.B TC08_IMAGE1
Path to the unit1 DECtape image (default
.BR media/tape1.tu56 ).
Created if missing; read/write.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Bootstrap block 0 from unit0 (OS/8 layout):
.EX
/ 1. set transfer address
cla cma           / AC=7777 if desired
dtca             \fR/ 6762\fP
cla
tad addr         / AC <- buffer start
dtxa             \fR/ 6771\fP
/ 2. start read of block 0, unit0
cla              / AC=0 selects unit0 block0 read
dtlb             \fR/ 6766\fP
/ 3. skip if ready; error if no skip
dtsf             \fR/ 6764\fP
.
addr,            / buffer lives here (256 words)
.EE
.TP
Write block 1 to unit1:
.EX
cla
tad addr         / AC <- buffer start
dtxa             \fR/ 6771\fP
cla
tad (1)          / block 1
tls              / ensure AC clean if needed
tlc
tad (02000)      / set unit1 bit
tad (04000)      / set write bit
dtlb             \fR/ 6766\fP
.EE
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B src/emulator/tc08_device.c
Device implementation.
.TP
.B src/emulator/tc08_device.h
IOT codes and public API.
.TP
.B factory/test_tc08.py
Python smoke tests for DTSF and unit1 write/readback.
.
